= Solution
{parent=iii}

Varying the quadratic action gives
$$
(z^2\mathcal R')'-z^2\nabla^2\mathcal R=0.
$$
For a Fourier mode,
$$
\boxed{\mathcal R_k''+2\frac{z'}z\mathcal R_k'
+k^2\mathcal R_k=0}.
$$
At late times $\epsilon\propto a^{-6}$, so
$$
z=a\sqrt{2\epsilon}\propto a^{-2}\propto\eta^2,
\qquad
\boxed{\frac{z'}z\simeq\frac2\eta}.
$$
The equation becomes $\mathcal R_k''+4\mathcal R_k'/\eta+k^2\mathcal R_k=0$. At $k=0$, its independent solutions are a constant and $\eta^{-3}$. The leading late-time solution in the form given in the question is therefore
$$
\boxed{\mathcal R_k(\eta)
=A_k\frac{1+ik\eta}{\eta^3}e^{-ik\eta}},
\qquad
\boxed{q=3}.
$$
This is the <growing curvature perturbation in ultra-slow-roll inflation>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= iv
{parent=2}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=iv}

Expand the quantized field using the normalized mode
$$
u_k(\eta)=A_k\frac{1+ik\eta}{\eta^3}e^{-ik\eta}.
$$
The <canonical commutation relation> fixes the Wronskian $M_{\rm Pl}^2z^2(u_ku_k^{*\prime}-u_k^*u_k')=i$. Writing $x=k\eta$, the primed correlators are
$$
\boxed{\langle\mathcal R\mathcal R\rangle'
=\frac{|A_k|^2}{\eta^6}(1+x^2)},
$$
$$
\boxed{\langle\mathcal R\dot{\mathcal R}\rangle'
=\frac{H|A_k|^2}{\eta^6}
(3+2x^2-ix^3)},
$$
$$
\boxed{\langle\dot{\mathcal R}\dot{\mathcal R}\rangle'
=\frac{H^2|A_k|^2}{\eta^6}
(9+3x^2+x^4)}.
$$
Each unprimed expression includes $(2\pi)^3\delta^{(3)}(\mathbf k+\mathbf k')$. The imaginary part of the mixed correlator gives
$$
|\langle[\mathcal R,\dot{\mathcal R}]\rangle'|
=\frac{2H|A_k|^2}{|\eta|^6}|x|^3.
$$
Consequently the <classicality parameter of a cosmological perturbation> is
$$
\boxed{\mathcal C(k,\eta)=
\frac{2|k\eta|^3}
{\sqrt{(1+k^2\eta^2)(9+3k^2\eta^2+k^4\eta^4)}}}
\simeq\frac23|k\eta|^3.
$$
It tends to zero on superhorizon scales, so the perturbation becomes effectively classical even while its amplitude grows as $a^3$. In ordinary slow-roll inflation, $\mathcal R$ instead freezes to a constant; its analogous normalized commutator also vanishes, but behaves as $|k\eta|$ for the leading de Sitter mode rather than $|k\eta|^3$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

